Delete the wedge geometry (raceParticles.js:154-201) and replace the whole system with ONE screen-space quad + fragment shader — same 1 draw call, zero new bytes.

Geometry: `new THREE.PlaneGeometry(2,2)`, ShaderMaterial with vertex shader `gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0); vUv = uv;` (true NDC quad, immune to fov/aspect changes), `blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending`, `depthTest:false`, `depthWrite:false`, `transparent:true`, `frustumCulled:false`, parented to the camera at any z, `renderOrder: 60`.

Fragment shader (polar streak field):
```
vec2 p = (vUv - uFocus) * vec2(uAspect, 1.0);
float r = length(p);
float a = atan(p.y, p.x);
float lane = floor(a / 6.2831853 * uLanes);
float h = fract(sin(lane * 91.7) * 43758.5453);
float af = fract(a / 6.2831853 * uLanes) - 0.5;
// angular profile: thin, soft-edged
float ang = exp(-af * af * 90.0);
// radial streak scrolling OUTWARD, tapered at both ends
float s = fract(r * uDensity - uTime * (2.6 + h * 1.8) - h);
float body = smoothstep(0.0, 0.12, s) * smoothstep(1.0, 0.55, s);
// keep the centre of frame clean, run past the corners
float mask = smoothstep(uInner, uInner + 0.22, r) * smoothstep(1.30, 0.95, r);
float i = ang * body * mask * uIntensity;
gl_FragColor = vec4(mix(vec3(1.0), uTint, 0.55) * i, i);
```
Uniforms: `uLanes = 34.0`, `uDensity = 2.6`, `uInner = 0.52`, `uAspect = w/h` (update on resize), `uFocus` = the projected look-ahead point in UV space (fall back to vec2(0.5,0.5)) so the streaks converge on where the kart is going, not on the screen centre, `uTint` = DRIFT_FEEL.sparkColors[miniTurboTier] (#00E5FF / #FFD34F / #C879FF) or #BFEAFF for pad boosts, `uTime` advanced by dt (never Math.random per frame), `uIntensity` from finding #2.

In raceParticles.js `update()`, replace the boolean with an envelope + overspeed term:
```
// module state
let boostEnergy = 0;
let punch = 0;
let wasBoosting = false;
// in update()
const over = clamp((context.speed - 0.80 * context.maxSpeed) / (0.30 * context.maxSpeed), 0, 1);
const want = context.boosting ? over : 0;
if (context.boosting && !wasBoosting) punch = 1;      // rising edge
wasBoosting = context.boosting;
punch = Math.max(0, punch - dt / 0.14);
const rate = want > boostEnergy ? dt / 0.07 : dt / 0.26;  // fast attack, slow release
boostEnergy += Math.sign(want - boostEnergy) * Math.min(rate, Math.abs(want - boostEnergy));
const intensity = clamp(boostEnergy * 0.85 + punch * 0.75, 0, 1.6);
speedLines.visible = intensity > 0.01 && !context.reducedMotion;
mat.uniforms.uIntensity.value = intensity;
mat.uniforms.uTime.value += dt;
```
